# Combo Design System – Cursor Rules

This file is the **permanent and strict standard** for this repository. All frontend work (components, pages, styles) must follow these guidelines.

---

## 1. Framework & Architecture (Angular)

- Use **Angular Standalone Components** only (`standalone: true`).
- Use **modern Angular Control Flow** syntax: `@if`, `@for`, `@switch` instead of `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, `*ngSwitch`.
- Prefer **`inject()`** for dependency injection over constructor injection.
- Implement proper lifecycle hooks and interfaces (e.g. `OnInit`, `ControlValueAccessor` for form inputs).

---

## 2. Design System & Shared Components

- **Always check** `src/app/shared/components/` for existing components (e.g. `combo-button`, `combo-input`, `combo-radio`, `shop-card`) before creating new raw HTML or PrimeNG elements.
- **Prefix** new custom components with `combo-` (e.g. `combo-checkbox`, `combo-select`).
- **Design aesthetic:** Keep a clean, minimalist design. Avoid colorful or busy backgrounds; action boxes and main containers must use a clean white background or specified neutral design tokens.

---

## 3. Mandatory UI/UX Rules

### Icons
- **Never use generic gift icons.** Always use the **specific app icon** for the feature or context (e.g. app-defined gift/promo icon from assets).

### Backgrounds
- **Action boxes must strictly have a white background.** Use design tokens (e.g. `var(--Combo-bg-background-white)` or equivalent).
- Maintain a clean design by **completely avoiding colorful or busy backgrounds** for main content areas and action containers.

### Typography & Headers
- **Welcome messages and header titles** must strictly use **primary, black, and light gray** colors from the design tokens (e.g. `var(--Combo-text-text-primary)`, `var(--Combo-text-text-default)`, neutral/light gray tokens).
- Do not introduce arbitrary or decorative colors for headings and welcome text.

---

## 4. CSS/SCSS Styling & Methodology

- Use **SCSS only** for styling.
- **Prefer Bootstrap utilities and Combo mixins** to minimize custom SCSS:
  - Use `d-flex`, `flex-column`, `align-items-*`, `justify-content-*`, `gap-*`, `position-absolute`, etc. (Bootstrap)
  - Use `combo-p-*`, `combo-m-*`, `combo-fs-*`, `combo-br-*`, `combo-w-*`, `combo-he-*`, `font-bold`, `font-medium` (from `src/assets/styles/mixins/`)
  - Keep SCSS only for: design tokens (colors, borders), hover/active/disabled states, line-clamp, transitions, and properties not covered by utilities.
- Follow **BEM (Block Element Modifier)** for custom HTML when adding component-specific classes:
  - Block: `.shop-card`
  - Element: `.shop-card__logo-wrapper`
  - Modifier: `.shop-card--active`
- **No hardcoded colors or sizes.** Use CSS variables from Design Tokens only, e.g.:
  - `var(--Combo-text-text-primary)`
  - `var(--Combo-bg-background-white)`
  - `var(--Combo-primary, #00846A)` when a fallback is required.
- **Avoid `::ng-deep`** on custom elements. Use it **only** when overriding third-party libraries (e.g. PrimeNG).

---

## 5. PrimeNG Usage & Overrides

- Assume PrimeNG may run in **Unstyled Mode** or with Tailwind resets.
- When styling/overriding PrimeNG:
  1. Wrap overrides in **`:host ::ng-deep { ... }`**.
  2. Prefer **data attributes** for targeting where possible (e.g. `[data-pc-section="page"]`, `[data-p-highlight="true"]`) in addition to or instead of generic classes like `.p-paginator-page`.
  3. Use **`!important`** only when necessary to override PrimeNG’s default theme.

---

## 6. Component Fallbacks & States

- Implement **graceful fallbacks** (e.g. missing image/logo: show a circle with the first two initials of the name).
- Handle **all states**: Default, Hover, Active/Checked, Disabled.

---

## 7. Response & Code Quality

- When creating or updating a component, provide **`.ts`**, **`.html`**, and **`.scss`** clearly separated.
- Keep code **clean**, **well-commented**, and **free of unnecessary console logs**.
